# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and captured traffic — the rules that matter most.
#
# This project's whole point is stopping confidential data leaving through AI
# tooling. A leak in its own repo would be the worst possible advertisement.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Real captured request bodies. These contain the developer's real
# account_uuid / device_id / session_id and whatever conversation was in
# flight — potentially credentials pulled out of tool_result blocks.
# NEVER commit these. The sanitised sample_* fixtures are committed instead;
# they have the same wire shape with entirely synthetic identifiers.
fixtures/*
!fixtures/.gitkeep
!fixtures/sample_*.json
!fixtures/README.md
!fixtures/placeholder_passport.txt
DEMO-RISKS.md

# Bearer tokens and the account_uuid -> bus identity map. Both are per-developer
# and both carry real identifiers. Commit the .example.json files instead.
store/config/api_tokens.json
store/config/account_map.json
**/config/*.local.json

# Environment files (DATABASE_URL, MCP_API_TOKEN, ...)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
store/.env

# Raw ingest payloads written before validation — may hold anything a caller sent.
store/bronze/
bronze/

# Drafts awaiting human approval, and debug payload dumps. Both are runtime
# state under /tmp by default, but do not commit them if the paths are moved.
dp_pending/
dp_outbound_debug*.json
dp_debug.log
dp_trace_gateway.log
dp_trace_store.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated artefacts & logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/usage_log.jsonl
docs/measurement-table.md
PASS

